  "title": "[Evidence] DIR-069: DIR-069: True 10/10 Parity — DOCX Multi-Page Full-Width Reflow, Photo Embedding, Archetype 2-Col Certs, Recruiter Application Export Gate, and Free-Tier Watermark",
  "sender": "STAFF_DEVELOPER",
  "directiveId": "DIR-069",
  "summary": "DIR-069 COMPLETE - true DOCX/PDF parity across six mandates plus the recruiter draft gate. (1) MULTI-PAGE FULL-WIDTH REFLOW: docxExport.js previously emitted ONE Section whose children were a single 2-column table, so Word reserved the 34% sidebar band on EVERY page. Added splitHeroForPageOne (a conservative node-height budget of 12200 twips) and twoColumnWithReflow; the Modern Split, Executive Banner and Tech Grid builders now return { children, continuation }, and resumeDocument emits the continuation as a SECOND Section with SectionType.NEXT_PAGE so page 2+ is 100 percent full width, matching the PDF smart-main-content--full. A one-page resume stays a single section. (2) ARCHETYPE CERT PARITY: the two buildCertificationsBlock calls in buildExecutiveBannerDocument and buildTechGridDocument flipped from columns 1 to columns 2, so every archetype matches the PDF 2-column card grid. (3) PHOTO EMBEDDING: imported ImageRun and added decodeDataUrlPhoto (validated image/png or image/jpeg base64 with a 2MB cap), fetchRemotePhoto (https-only against a 3-host image-CDN allowlist, redirect disabled, 5s timeout, 2MB cap, image/* content-type required) and buildPhotoParagraph; buildIdentityHeader leads with the headshot (so the sidebar header variant inherits it), and resolveResumePhoto runs in createResumeDocx before the synchronous build. Any failure, including a non-allowlisted or loopback host, is non-fatal and the photo is simply omitted. (4) SKILL PILLS: non-inline skills are no longer raw bullets; they render as shaded F1F5F9 pill runs with padding, keeping the inline and rating variants and a linear reading order. (5) FREE-TIER WATERMARK: when resume._watermark.enableFreeWatermark is true the section footer carries the branded 'Created with IME365 (Free Plan)' tag; both DOCX routes now compute the same isPaidOwner flag the PDF route uses, so free-tier DOCX matches the PDF (a branded footer tag, which the mandate explicitly permits as an alternative to a diagonal watermark). (6) RECRUITER DRAFT GATE: POST /api/public-export-docx now has an explicit, server-verified employer-claim branch - when the caller is authenticated and supplies jobId plus applicationId, the server re-verifies job.employerId === req.user.uid AND that the application belongs to that job AND that its resumeId equals the requested resumeId AND then loads the draft resume; every other request keeps the strict published-only rule. I did NOT simply delete the published-only check (that would have been a real IDOR hole). The drawer now forwards the claim (jobId/applicationId) through exportDownloader, so the path is wired end to end. (7) GUARDS: src/cv-templates git diff = 0, 100 percent Linux compatible, zero OS console windows. EVIDENCE: new tests/dir069-docx-parity.test.mjs 13/13 - static contracts for all seven mandates plus FUNCTIONAL proofs: a data-URL photo lands in word/media with a w:drawing and its absence produces no media part; a loopback photo URL is refused and the export still succeeds; the watermark reaches word/footer1.xml while a paid export has none; skills emit w:fill=F1F5F9; a 24-role resume emits a nextPage section while a one-page resume does not; executive-banner and tech-grid emit equal-width 2-column certification card tables; and the drawer forwards the employer claim. Regression: dir063..069 + previews + empty-sections + dir048/055/056 + employer + fouc 153/153; backend DOCX/parity/export-pipeline 38/38; full control surface 2090/2090; product + design-system + dashboard + employer slice 147/147. GATES: lint 0 errors (253 pre-existing warnings); security:static 67/67; xampp-policy 4/4; build 'built in 2.98s' (under the 4.0s budget); headless Playwright DOM census on gridDense PASS (0px footer overlap across 55 templates); overflow probe on long 0 failures. SUPERSEDED CONTRACTS UPDATED: dir067 S4 and dir068 previously asserted that the public DOCX route never reads req.user.uid; DIR-069 legitimately requires that read inside the verified employer claim, so both now assert the stronger contract - the only owner read is the job-ownership check, and the published-only rule remains the fallback. HONEST LIMITS: (a) the page-1/continuation split is a conservative node-height HEURISTIC, not a paginator, so a pathological page-1 overflow could still carry the table onto page 2; (b) the free-tier DOCX mark is a branded FOOTER TAG, not a true Word diagonal watermark; (c) photo support is base64 data URLs plus a 3-host image-CDN allowlist - other hosts (including the app's own storage origin) are refused and the photo is omitted; (d) the recruiter draft gate is IDOR-safe by construction and unit-verified, but I did NOT exercise a live authenticated draft export against a live MariaDB; (e) scripts/verify-zero-broken-routes.mjs and tests/full-system-audit.mjs need a live host and were not run."
}